# BUGS

The canonical form is written but not checked: a directory whose records are out of order, or which names an entry twice, is read if it hashes to its name, and a lookup finds the first entry of a name.
The permission bits of `mode` are not checked either, so a directory may carry modes vxstore never writes.

distd(8) reads an index or a directory whole into a buffer of 68 KiB, so it cannot serve a file larger than about 135 MiB, nor a directory of more than some 600 entries.
